      "problem": "Find the value of $170 - 281.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $281$ is larger than $170,$ the answer will be negative.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem:\n\n$$\n281 - 170\n$$\n\nNext, we carry out the subtraction:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14132866/assets/56c6cf2342749514e74235f5f8635b421137814ba344a74745cf15ec0f396f93.svg)\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n281-170 = 111.\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n170 - 281 = -111.\n$$",
